    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="0732" n="1466" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1466"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Terrell.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 810.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 758, of the 6th instant, inclosing copy of a dispatch from the British
                    consul at Erzeroum to the British ambassador at Constantinople, relating to the
                    position of American missionaries at Bitlis.</p>
                <pb facs="0733" n="1467" xml:id="pg1467"/>
                <p>The considerate kindness of the British ambassador and of Mr. Oumberbatch in
                    furnishing information of this character is highly-appreciated.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
